      "writtenOn": "2014-03-25T23:12:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure, that\u0027s true. FWIW the entire python-ldap API could probably be reduced to 1/3 it\u0027s current size because there are a lot methods which simply call their sister entry point which have additional parameters. But to understand which methods can be substituted one has to look at the API implementation.\n\nI can see an argument for retaining the simple entry points which are the ones used 99% of the time but I\u0027m not wed to that. If you feel strongly we can remove the \"simple\" entry points and only keep the more functional entry points. At the moment I\u0027m leaning to keeping the simple entry points.",
